      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me look at the `AbstractStringEncoderTest` to understand `checkEncodingVariations`.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that 41 different names all produce the Soundex code \"B650\". The main readability issue is the massive flat inline list on one line. I'll improve it by:\n1. Adding a descriptive comment\n2. Extracting the names into a well-formatted array variableThe improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version extracts the 41 names into a clearly grouped `namesEncodingToB650` array with inline comments explaining each phonetic family (Bar-/Bir-, Bra-/Bre-, Bro-, Bru-, By-, etc.), adds a Javadoc comment explaining what Soundex code B650 represents, and introduces an `expectedCode` variable — all while calling `checkEncodingVariations` with identical arguments and producing the same runtime behavior."
